Installed `Handwriting` (`@/components/ui/handwriting`), a thin wrapper over the `tegaki` renderer with the Caveat font.

```tsx
import { Handwriting } from "@/components/ui/handwriting";

<Handwriting className="text-5xl">Hello, world</Handwriting>
```

Size and color follow the text styles. Change the text to write it again.

Complex shaping (ligatures, contextual alternates, Arabic and Indic scripts) is opt-in: `npm i harfbuzzjs`, then register the shaper once, in the browser:

```tsx
import { TegakiEngine } from "tegaki/react";

useEffect(() => {
  import("tegaki/shaper-harfbuzz").then((m) => TegakiEngine.registerShaper(m.default));
}, []);
```

Next.js (Turbopack) also needs `turbopack: { resolveAlias: { module: { browser: "./src/lib/empty-module.ts" } } }` with an empty module there: harfbuzzjs imports Node's `module` on its server branch.

Vite dev server (Vite 7 or older): add `optimizeDeps: { exclude: ["tegaki", "harfbuzzjs"] }` so the font and WASM files keep their URLs. Astro: add `tegaki()` from `tegaki/astro/integration` when it renders on the server.

Font data carries its font's license: Caveat is SIL OFL 1.1 (Copyright 2014 The Caveat Project Authors). Wraps Tegaki by Gokhan Kurt (MIT); the license notice is at the end of the file.
